- [Dokku](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/cloud-platforms/dokku.md): Deploy ParadeDB on Dokku
- [DigitalOcean](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/cloud-platforms/digitalocean.md): Deploy ParadeDB on DigitalOcean
- [High Availability](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/self-hosted/high-availability.md): Use read replicas to minimize downtime in production
- [Getting Started](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/logical-replication/getting-started.md): Configure ParadeDB as a logical subscriber of an existing Postgres primary
- [Initial Sync and Indexing](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/logical-replication/bootstrapping.md): Wait for the initial copy, build ParadeDB indexes, and query replicated data
- [Replication Configuration](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/logical-replication/configuration.md): Configure publication boundaries, replication capacity, and replica identity
- [Schema Changes](https://www.paradedb.com/docs/operate/deploy/logical-replication/schema-changes.md): Add replicated tables and safely apply schema changes
